Track 2: Cardboard Telescopes Chew the North Star
- Story & Context: Balanced precarious atop an Oji apartment roof with a home-assembled cardboard reflector telescope, synthesist Aoi Moriyama recorded her confession of grief over two lost notebooks swept off a pier during the transatlantic expedition. She tuned her electric lap steel to an open D-minor, letting the bottleneck drag across the nickel strings in microtonal sobs that mimicked the groaning buoyancy tanks of submersibles. During the second verse, a stray gust from an approaching typhoon knocked over their kerosene stove and scorched the microphone stand, yet she didn't flinch, singing the tearful refrain: "We squint through folded paper tubes, but you are still submerged."
