Track 3: Who Cut the Moon’s Return Path?
- Story & Context: The final cut addresses the urban myth of the 2021 equinox blackout, when a severed undersea trunk off Nova Scotia caused three Yokohama pirate stations to simultaneously broadcast the same spectral steel guitar phrase. Producer Kenjiro reconstructed the mythic night by sampling acoustic pressure bursts recorded by retired cable repairmen, burying the track's chorus under five cascading layers of tape flanging and hyper-fast liquid percussion. As the legendary final breakdown fades, Moriyama's pitch-shifted vocal asks over a lonely weeping slide: "If you cut the glass line beneath the sand, where does our laughter bounce?"
